Derived from codex-plugin-cc:
- the companion-script layout (scripts/agy-companion.mjs and its subcommands)
  and scripts/stop-review-gate-hook.mjs, whose hook-input reading, decision
  emitting, and gate-then-review control flow are adapted from upstream's
  script of the same job
- scripts/lib/stop-review.mjs: its ALLOW:/BLOCK: first-line parsing is a
  close line-for-line match of upstream's parseStopReviewOutput, which lives
  inline in the hook script there rather than in a file of its own
- scripts/lib/prompts.mjs (prompt file loading by name and placeholder
  interpolation by regex replace)
- scripts/lib/state.mjs (per-workspace state under the plugin data directory,
  including the workspace-root hashing and slugging)
- the command, skill and agent structure under commands/, skills/, agents/

Not derived, despite the name match: scripts/lib/process.mjs and
scripts/lib/workspace.mjs share only the job their upstream namesakes do
(spawning a command without a shell; resolving the workspace root with a
fallback to the given directory). The code differs throughout; both were
written from scratch to solve problems upstream's versions do not have
(Windows .cmd/.bat shim resolution; avoiding a shell-out to git). They are
named here, not for licence purposes, but so a reader comparing file lists
is not left wondering why two obviously matching names are missing from the
list above.

Everything else in this repository, including the two files just named, is
the work of its author and is offered under the MIT License in LICENSE. The
Apache-2.0 terms continue to apply to the derived parts listed above.
